think guidance page. Each reading is one `grep` over the whole list instead, following the idiom
think `tame_style_scan_advise.rish` already uses: five processes rather than four thousand.
think Walls and ratchets split on whether a red would land on ordinary work. `qualified_assert`
think reads 0 of 1,073 and `tame_style_check` already bans the spelling, so a wall records a fact.
think The print bind TAME asks for as-you-touch and gates nowhere, so 118 is a ratchet or it is a
think guard somebody turns off.
think Kept the elder 24 walled by name on all four duties. A ratchet alone would let one of them
think regress under a falling ceiling and say nothing, and accrete-never-break says what was
think already proven stays proven.

obs THE 25 WAS NEVER A FILE COUNT. The elder witness printed `length lines result.out` and said
obs "all 25 hosted files"; the list holds 24 paths and the twenty-fifth was the trailing empty
obs line. `context/TAME_CORE.md`, `construction/standing-equipment.kyri` and my own last session
obs log all carried the 25, copied forward since `20260729.230300`. A guard reporting its own
obs output length is measuring the instrument rather than the tree -- which is this widening one
obs layer down, and it is why I counted the list by hand before writing the number.
obs I did not book it as a red. It was wrong on three living pages for a year, and all three are
obs repaired in this commit; the pin reads `rows_that_fit=0` and two ships have already surfaced
obs that to Keaton. A row I cannot file and have already fixed is an account, not an allocation.
obs THE CONTROL'S FIRST DRAFT PROVED NOTHING TWICE. `roster_comment_stripped` was derived from the
obs same clean-file count as `clean_counted_hosted`, so it could not have failed while its neighbor
obs passed -- one reading wearing two names. Repaired by planting a real second room holding a real
obs hosted file and naming it on a comment line: stripped, the count stays 1. Proven from the
obs failing side by removing the strip from a copy of the scan, where it reads `no` while
obs `clean_counted_hosted` still reads `yes`.
obs AND THE CONTROL PAID THE PER-ITEM FORK ITSELF. Its first draft re-ran the whole scan for every
obs field it wanted, so a case asking five fields paid five scans: 22.7s against a witness that had
obs cost 966ms. One scan per planted state brought it to 19.6s, of which the scan proper is 1.3s.
obs That is diffuser's own `20260908` finding arriving in my lane one hour later, and I paid it
obs before shipping rather than after.
obs AGAINST MYSELF, TWICE, ON THE BATON'S OWN CLAUSES. I launched the cold pass with `nohup ... &`
obs inside a tool call; the launching shell exited, the process group leader went with it, and the
obs pass ran on as an orphan holding the run lock while its output reached nobody. The runner
obs diagnosed it exactly -- `run_lock=in_flight`, `group_leader=gone`, `lap=gone` -- and printed
obs the repair, which worked first try. That is the same detached-launch shape COPAL's `set -m`
obs fix closed in the control this morning, met from the launcher's side.
obs Then I typed `pgrep -fa standing_equipment_run` to find it, and the answer named seven peer
obs trees. Read-only, so nothing was harmed, and it is precisely the reflex the baton names as the
obs family's sixth firing. `fleet_call.sh --pattern` refused 14 foreign processes by working
obs directory and sent to the 2 in this tree.

